## Why This Is Asked
This question tests practical mastery of real-time React patterns: useSyncExternalStore integration, per-context memoization, and cross-tab coordination, all with efficient rendering via virtualization.

## Key Concepts
- useSyncExternalStore for a per-workspace stream
- memoized selectors with bounded caches (LRU)
- React.memo for item components and react-window for list virtualization
- BroadcastChannel for cross-tab acknowledgments
- cleanup on workspace switch and basic backpressure handling

## Code Example
```javascript
// Skeleton selector cache (conceptual)
class SelectorCache {
  constructor(limit = 100) {
    this.limit = limit
    this.map = new Map();
  }
  get(key) {
    const v = this.map.get(key);
    if (!v) return undefined;
    // simple LRU touch
    this.map.delete(key);
    this.map.set(key, v);
    return v;
  }
  set(key, value) {
    if (this.map.has(key)) {
      this.map.delete(key);
    } else if (this.map.size >= this.limit) {
      const firstKey = this.map.keys().next().value;
      this.map.delete(firstKey);
    }
    this.map.set(key, value);
  }
}
```

